    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d398">

                <pb facs="0593" n="519" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg519"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Williams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 165.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 26, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your despatch of the 10th of March, No. 24,
                    has been received.</p>
                <p>It will be entirely agreeable to this government that I receive and afford all
                    desirable facilities to the agent of Prince Kung. I trust that the observations
                    he may be able to make in the western nations will be productive of results
                    beneficial as well to these nations as to his own great and very interesting
                    country.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. Wells Williams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
